## In-app map (osmdroid / OpenStreetMap)

User-requested, key-free in-app map (no Google Maps SDK / API key):

- Added `org.osmdroid:osmdroid-android` (catalog + app build). Only INTERNET is
  needed (already present); the tile cache is app-internal and the OSM
  user-agent is set to the package id.
- `ui/venuemap/VenueOsmMap.kt`: a lifecycle-managed `MapView` wrapped in
  `AndroidView` — `VenueOsmMap` (read-only camp + category-tinted pin markers,
  tap → select) and `VenueOsmPicker` (interactive, reports its centre as the
  user pans, for the editor crosshair).
- Viewer: an **Illustration / Map** `SingleChoiceSegmentedButtonRow` (mirrors iOS
  `VenueMapMode`). Map mode shows the embedded OSM map centred on the camp /
  selected pin; empty-state when nothing has a coordinate. The content sits in a
  `weight(1f)` region so the full-bleed map never overlaps the segmented control.
- Editor: the "Set map location" sheet is now an interactive osmdroid map with a
  fixed centre crosshair (pan so the marker sits on the spot → "Use this
  location"), replacing the manual lat/lon fields. Removed the now-unused
  lat/lon/use-camp strings.

## D5 Venue Map

iOS is the source of truth — ported `VenueMapModels`, `VenueMapService`,
`VenueMapObserver`, `VenueMapView`, `VenueMapEditorView`, the pin
sheets/components, and the `CampingDetailView` entry points.

- **Model**: `VenueMap` + `VenuePoint` + `VenueMapPayload`/`toVenueMap` already
  existed (A10). Extended in place with derived helpers (`hasImage`,
  `hasContent`, `pointsOnIllustration`, `pointsWithCoordinate`,
  `VenuePoint.hasImagePosition`/`hasCoordinate`). No duplication.
- **Service** (`data/venuemap/VenueMapService.kt`): interface + Firestore (live
  `config` listener via `callbackFlow`, `VenueMapPayload` write with
  `imageURL`/`imagePublicID` delete-when-empty + `updatedAt` serverTimestamp) +
  in-memory `FakeVenueMapService` + Hilt binding. Path
  `campings/{id}/venueMap/config`.
- **ViewModel** (`ui/venuemap/VenueMapViewModel.kt`): one VM for both screens,
  sealed `VenueMapUiState` (Loading/Error/Ready). A single owned listener keeps
  the embedded pin set live; every pin/image mutation rewrites the full config
  doc. `canManage = canManageTeams || canManageSchedule`. Site image uploaded via
  the shared backend-signed `ImageUploader` (Cloudinary).
- **Viewer** (`VenueMapScreen.kt`): 4:3 Coil site image with pins positioned at
  `imageX`/`imageY`, tappable detail card, "Locations" legend, empty state
  (managers get "Build the map"). Coordinate pins offer **Open in Maps** (a
  `geo:` intent) — the Android-native stand-in for the iOS MapKit overlay +
  directions.
- **Editor** (`VenueMapEditorScreen.kt`, gated `canManage` else Restricted):
  upload/replace/remove the site illustration (photo picker → Cloudinary),
  tap-to-place / reposition pins on the canvas, per-pin overflow
  (edit/reposition/set map location/delete), pin editor `ModalBottomSheet`
  (name + category chips + note) and a coordinate sheet (lat/lon entry, "use camp
  location", clear).
- **Camp detail** (`CampingDetailScreen.kt`): the header location chip
  (pin + place name) deep-links to the venue map (mirrors iOS `headerSection`),
  and a self-silencing `VenueMapEntryCard` appears in the body when the map has
  content (the detail VM now loads the map one-shot to drive it). `VenuePointDetailCard`
  composites the translucent `surface` token over `background` so the floating
  card is opaque.
- **Program↔venue link** (`ui/schedule/`): the program editor offers the camp's
  pins as FilterChips; picking one sets `venuePointID` + fills `location` with
  the pin name, typing a custom location clears `venuePointID`. The schedule
  service already wrote `venuePointID` delete-when-empty.
- **Navigation**: typed routes `AppRoute.CampingVenueMap` /
  `CampingVenueMapEditor`, two `composable` destinations (viewer ↔ editor).
- **i18n**: venue strings added to EN, FR, PT-BR (incl. a `venue_card_subtitle`
  plural with `one`/`many`/`other`).

## Data contract

- Single doc `venueMap/config`; `imageURL`/`imagePublicID` delete-when-empty;
  `points[]` element `id`/`name` (req; dropped if missing)/`category` (raw)
  /`note` (`""`)/`imageX`/`imageY` (0…1, omit-when-nil)/`latitude`/`longitude`
  (omit-when-nil); `updatedAt` serverTimestamp on every write. `program.venuePointID`
  delete-when-empty, pin `name` kept in `program.location`.

## Notes / deviations (iOS authoritative)

- The embedded map + crosshair coordinate picker are ported via **osmdroid /
  OpenStreetMap** (key-free) instead of Apple/Google Maps. Still deferred: the
  live user-location dot and in-app MKDirections turn-by-turn routing — pin
  directions defer to the device maps app via the `geo:` intent. The data
  contract (real coordinates per pin) is unchanged.
